### Food Delivery Platform - API Gateway
### Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Start the gateway first:  .\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123
# The access token of step 0 (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that)
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 0. Admin login (needs user-service) -> adminToken, for the routes and the admin calls below
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

### 1. Gateway health (expect: {"status":"UP"})
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/health

### 2. Application info
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/info

### 3. All configured routes (path -> microservice): administrators only (401 without a token, 403 for another role)
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/gateway/routes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4. Request id is generated: check the X-Request-Id response header
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/health

### 5. Your own request id is kept and forwarded to the service
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/health
X-Request-Id: my-test-request-001

### 6. Path without a route (expect: 404)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/unknown

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Routed calls. They return 5xx until the target service exists and is running.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### user-service (Phase 2)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/users?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### restaurant-service (Phase 3)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants

### catalog-service (Phase 4)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/categories

### order-service (Phase 5)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/orders?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### payment-service (Phase 6)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/payments?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### delivery-service (Phase 10), search-service (Phase 11)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/search/restaurants?q=biryani

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Rate limiting (Phase 12): Redis token buckets per signed-in user (per client IP for a visitor). Responses carry X-RateLimit-* headers.
### Every route: 20 requests/second (bursts up to 40). Login and registration: 10 per minute
### (120 in docker-compose, so the test scripts can sign up many users). Over the limit: 429 Too Many Requests.
### Send this one repeatedly and watch X-RateLimit-Remaining drop, then the 429.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Login budget
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "wrong-password" }

### The buckets in Redis (direct): docker exec -it fd-redis redis-cli --scan --pattern "request_rate_limiter*"
